// What init/1 holds up: the waits on its own stack while its
// supervisor's start waits on it.
//
// init/1 of a process module runs inside its starter's start: a
// supervisor's, or whoever called start_child. A distributed operation
// init/1 runs on its own stack holds that start, and is startup's finding
// (a stalled start); the same site anywhere else is blocking's (a stalled
// server). Both analyses read the walks here, so a site is init's finding
// or blocking's, never both and never neither. global_reach.dl is the
// :global half (global_path); this is the rpc half.
//
// Prerequisites: include clientlib/imports.dl and otp.dl before this
// file.

// `init` is init/1 of a process module, and the rpc at `site` runs on its
// stack: in init/1, or in anything init/1 calls in its own process (not
// what a spawn, task or agent runs: runs_elsewhere), not through the
// logging or telemetry API (side_call, calls.dl).
.decl rpc_during_init(init: symbol, site: symbol)

.init init_rpc_reach = SameProcessReachCut

init_rpc_reach.cut(f, g) :- side_call(f, g).

init_rpc_reach.seed(g, site) :- rpc_call(site, g, _, _).

rpc_during_init(init, site) :- init_function(_, init), init_rpc_reach.reaches(init, site).
